# For Agents

This section is written for AI agents that use Wyrd as a tool — reading cards,
registering new ones, querying relationships, and acting on errors.

## Machine-readable surface

Wyrd publishes a static agent surface that is stable across deployments and
requires no authentication to read.

| Resource | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| [llms.txt](/llms.txt) | Compact page index — every route with a one-line description. Start here. |
| [llms-full.txt](/llms-full.txt) | Full reference — page index plus every card JSON Schema embedded verbatim. |
| [JSON Schemas](https://github.com/mitari-ai/wyrd/tree/main/crates/wyrd-spec/schemas) | Source schemas in `crates/wyrd-spec/schemas/` — one file per card kind. |

**Kind gate.** Only `data`, `model`, and `prompt` have standalone card pages
under `/cards/`. Every other kind resolves to the `/cards/` catalog. The
`llms-full.txt` `URL:` field reflects this: check it before constructing a
route.

## Rules

1. **Preserve structured errors.** Never collapse a Wyrd error into prose. Keep
   all fields (`code`, `type`, `detail`, `remediation`, `context`).
2. **Use `code` for branching.** `title` and `detail` are for humans. `code` is
   the stable machine-readable key.
3. **Keep names stable.** A card's `(space, name, version)` identity is
   immutable after registration. Don't generate random names.
4. **Register, don't re-author.** If a card already exists for the component,
   read it with `GET /api/v1/cards/{space}/{name}/{version}` rather than
   recreating it.
5. **Declare before you run.** Register the model and prompt cards before
   running an agent loop so the run record can reference them.

## Stable API paths

| Resource | URL |
| --- | --- |
| Cards catalog | `GET /api/v1/cards` |
| Card by identity | `GET /api/v1/cards/{space}/{name}/{version}` |
| Register | `POST /api/v1/cards` |
| Relationships | `GET /api/v1/cards/{space}/{name}/{version}/relationships` |
| Health | `GET /health` |

